\begin_layout Standard
Video evidence revolves around established physics,
 not belief.
 In order to see what happened with the videos,
 you need to be familiar with the two kind of phenomena:
 explosion physics and ballistics physics.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
When a high kinetic energy object strikes a static object,
 momentum is transferred and mechanical joints within the structures are broken in a sequence of events some call deformations.
 The way these deformations evolve over time depends on many factors including the kind of materials,
 the kinetic energy of the colliding object,
 and so on,
 so there isn't one way to generalize all kinds of collisions.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
There are three physical phenomena important here that vary amongst explosions and ballistics:
 expanding energy,
 deforming materials,
 and sound emissions.
 This section does a very brief introduction to how they relate for explosions and ballistics.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Explosion Physics (Briefly)
