\begin_layout Subsection
Summary
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In other words,
 the physics of bullets and explosives work in opposite directions of the expanding material,
 expanding energy,
 and expanding vacuums.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
A bullet cavitation SUCKS before it BLOWS.
 The sounds you hear from a rifle bullet are known as a CRACK - THUMP.
 CRACK is the sound of the bullet hitting a body,
 in the case of a bullet hitting a human it's more like a meat slapping sound.
 After the bullet strikes,
 with a longer pause based on how far away the bullet was shot,
 there will be the report of the rifle as the sound from the gunpowder detonation arrives at the target.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
An explosion BLOWS then SUCKS.
 The sounds you hear is one powerful high frequency BOOM of the impulse expanding.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The velocity of detonation of gunpowder is around 200 m/s.
 The velocity of detonation of explosives like C4 is about 4000 m/s and SEMTEX is about 10,000 m/s.
 The energy released and the timeframes involved are orders of magnitude different from each other.
 
\end_layout

